From 9ef06057741f38ef775ec1655333be207d2b3d24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reid Smythe <rwsmythe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:38:02 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(wp6.5): build macOS arm64 GPL FFmpeg release/9.0 at
 b204e94e without zvbi

Clearwater WP6.5 (docs/briefs/wp6.5-brief.md in rwsmythe/clearwater), group 2a.
One commit on wp6.3c-nozvbi-r2 (d77b8352); the Windows recipe
(.github/workflows/build.yml, build.sh, scripts.d/ and the rest) is unchanged.

macos/build-script/ vendors the Riedl build script (Apache-2.0,
https://git.martin-riedl.de/ffmpeg/build-script, branch main at
f63b8aab8f5ce1a067da86ba69e34a36a7e217e5, 2026-08-17): LICENSE, build.sh,
script/functions.sh and the build-*.sh and version/* files of the components
this recipe builds (zvbi's are not vendored), byte-identical to that tree
with the same modes except these edits:
- script/functions.sh download(): looks up the sha256 of the exact URL in
  macos/sha256-pins.txt and ends the component on a missing pin or a
  mismatch (the script fetched every tarball without a checksum; a mismatch
  never falls back to a mirror).
- script/functions.sh prepareMeson(): uses the meson the workflow installs
  by hash instead of an unpinned "pip install meson" in a virtualenv (the
  runner's python3 has no virtualenv module and no meson).
- script/build-ffmpeg.sh: FFmpeg from git, release/9.0 checked out at
  b204e94e90fca64045e9ca7dd44c65678c7eb29e (the Windows pin; git checkout
  --detach fails the build if the commit is absent) instead of the 9.0.1
  release tarball named by version/ffmpeg (not vendored); --extra-version is
  the UTC build date (the Windows form) instead of https://www.martin-riedl.de;
  -FFMPEG_SNAPSHOT other than NO is refused.
- script/build-x264.sh: x264 from git at
  0480cb05fa188d37ae87e8f4fd8f1aea3711f7ee (master head, also the Windows
  pin) instead of the floating master archive.
- script/build-x265.sh: the maintainers' release file
  downloads/x265_4.2.tar.gz instead of the generated get/4.2.tar.gz (the
  same tree, but the generated archive's x265Version.txt reads releasetag
  4.0, so the library would report 4.0).
- script/build-x265.sh (also): every cmake call passes
  -DCMAKE_IGNORE_PREFIX_PATH="/opt/homebrew;/usr/local" (CMake adds
  Homebrew's prefix to its system search on macOS even when brew is off
  PATH, Modules/Platform/Darwin.cmake; no find may reach a host package).
- script/build-ninja.sh: -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF (ninja's CMakeLists includes
  CTest, searches an installed GTest and otherwise FetchContent-downloads
  GoogleTest outside download() and the pins) and the same
  CMAKE_IGNORE_PREFIX_PATH.
- script/build-cmake.sh: the fallback is the same release file
  cmake-4.0.3-macos-universal.tar.gz from cmake.org (the same sha256)
  instead of a source build (CMake's own configure runs with CTest on and
  searches host packages); a failed second download fails the build.
- script/build-nasm.sh: the fallback is the same release file
  nasm-3.02.tar.gz as archived by the Wayback Machine (the same sha256,
  with the generated configure) instead of GitHub's tag archive (no
  configure; its autogen.sh needs autotools the runner lacks); the
  autogen branch's checkStatus passes the status ($?) it lacked.
- script/build-harfbuzz.sh: meson runs with -Dfreetype=enabled (this
  build's freetype) and glib, gobject, cairo, chafa, icu, png, tests,
  introspection, docs, utilities and gpu_demo disabled (auto features
  only a host package could satisfy, and test / tool targets).

macos/sha256-pins.txt: the sha256 of the 18 URLs the vendored scripts can
request on macOS (fallback URLs included; each fallback serves the same
file as its primary). macos/meson-requirements.txt: meson
1.11.2 by hash (the newest release that runs on the Xcode python3 3.9).

.github/workflows/build-macos.yml: workflow_dispatch only; both jobs run
only in rwsmythe/FFmpeg-Builds; every action pinned to a 40-hex commit (no
floating tag from build.yml); permissions empty at the top. The build job
(macos-26, contents: read) runs the vendored script under env -i (PATH
without Homebrew, no PKG_CONFIG_* / CPATH / LIBRARY_PATH / *FLAGS from the
image, MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=14.0) with -SKIP_ZVBI=YES, -SKIP_DECKLINK=YES
and the components Clearwater does not use skipped (libklvanc, rav1e, srt,
zimg, libbluray, snappy, libvmaf, aom, dav1d, openh264, openjpeg, svt-av1,
libtheora, vpx, vvenc, libwebp, lame, opus, libvorbis), then fails unless
ffmpeg and ffprobe are arm64 Mach-O with minos 14.0, have an otool -L
record that lists libSystem and nothing outside /usr/lib and
/System/Library (a grep error fails too), report n9.0.2-47-gb204e94e...-<date> built from the pinned
FFmpeg and x264 commits, carry --enable-gpl --enable-version3
--enable-libx265 --enable-libx264 and not --enable-nonfree, libfdk,
--enable-libzvbi or --enable-decklink, and list the libx265,
hevc_videotoolbox, libx264 and aac encoders. The publish job (ubuntu-24.04,
contents: write) releases ONE archive
ffmpeg-n9.0.2-47-gb204e94e90-macos-arm64-gpl-9.0.zip (bin/ffmpeg,
bin/ffprobe, LICENSE.txt = FFmpeg's COPYING.GPLv3, build/ with the version,
encoder, dylib, toolchain and pin records and the component logs) plus
checksums.sha256 under the tag
ffmpeg-9.0-gb204e94e-macos-arm64-nozvbi-<commit7> created at this commit,
and checks the tag and the GitHub asset digest (the tag must be absent
beforehand: only an HTTP 404 from the lookup counts as absent).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
